;; FH-CALL-002 — vector-head classification is total.
;;
;; Three legal heads and one error arm, in this order, with no fourth case.
;; `:head` names a value the harness constructs (EDN cannot carry a live
;; descriptor or a function); `:expect` is the classification, or `:error`
;; plus the exact diagnostic id.
;;
;; The illegal rows are chosen to close the ways an implementation drifts
;; back to a heuristic: a plain function (the permissive bare-function
;; model), a plain map (IFn on both hosts, and the shape a descriptor
;; would take if it were data), and the scalar heads a hiccup walker is
;; tempted to stringify.
{:fh/id "FH-CALL-002"
 :fh/law
 "A Freehand descriptor is an internal boundary, a keyword is a DOM/custom element, a declared host descriptor is a foreign boundary, and anything else raises :rf.error/view-bad-head naming those three legal forms."

 :cases
 [{:head :fixture/declared-view    :expect :view}
  {:head :fixture/element-keyword  :expect :element}
  {:head :fixture/custom-element   :expect :element}
  {:head :fixture/host-descriptor  :expect :host}

  {:head :fixture/plain-function   :expect :error :error-id :rf.error/view-bad-head}
  {:head :fixture/string           :expect :error :error-id :rf.error/view-bad-head}
  {:head :fixture/nil              :expect :error :error-id :rf.error/view-bad-head}
  {:head :fixture/number           :expect :error :error-id :rf.error/view-bad-head}
  {:head :fixture/vector           :expect :error :error-id :rf.error/view-bad-head}
  {:head :fixture/plain-map        :expect :error :error-id :rf.error/view-bad-head}
  {:head :fixture/symbol           :expect :error :error-id :rf.error/view-bad-head}]

 ;; The message is stable in MEANING, not bytes. What it must always name:
 ;; all three legal forms, and — for a callable head — the helper recovery.
 :message-must-name        ["v/defview" "keyword" "host descriptor"]
 :callable-message-must-name ["parentheses"]

 :ex-data-keys [:rf.error/id :legal-heads :head :recovery]}
